On a base already red at sast (base/: an unused eval(), B307), this change adds an unused function calling exec() (B102). The base's finding is inherited; the new one is the diff's own, so sast is NO-GO with one finding introduced (docs/adr/0072 §1).
---
 app/backend/meetups/legacy.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py b/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py
index 5c43b56..166ebe0 100644
--- a/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py
+++ b/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py
@@ -8,3 +8,7 @@ before the change under test.
 
 def evaluate(expression: str) -> object:
     return eval(expression)
+
+
+def run(source: str) -> None:
+    exec(source)
